<title>HONG KONG: Shinhan Bank to set US$200 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>Shinhan Bank to set US$200 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shinhan Bank has verbally mandated Deutsche Morgan Grenfell and HSBC Markets to arrange a US$200 million floating rate note issue, bankers said.</p>
<p>The facility has a final maturity of three years with no put or call options.</p>
<p>The issue will be priced at 99.9875 percent of par to float at 12.5 basis points over the three-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>With fees, the all-in return for top-tier managers is 17.5 basis points.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
